---
const phases = [
  {
    state: 'Complete',
    tone: 'success',
    title: 'Foundation',
    body: 'Design system, component library, interactive showcase, documentation and CI for the iOS app — typechecked, linted, 210 tests, and a bundle export on every pull request.',
  },
  {
    state: 'In build',
    tone: 'primary',
    title: 'The product',
    body: 'Inventory on-device, offline-first, with the shopping list, reminders, receipt import and multi-device sync that make the foundation worth shipping.',
  },
  {
    state: 'Specified',
    tone: 'neutral',
    title: 'The service',
    body: 'A separate backend repository holds all product logic: the API contract, the data model with owner-scoped access rules, sync and the AI worker. It boots today; the routes are documented rather than live.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
  <div class="shell stack">
    <header class="section__head">
      <p class="t-overline">Status</p>
      <h2 class="t-title" id="status-title">Where the build stands</h2>
      <p class="t-lead measure">
        We would rather say this plainly than show you a mockup and call it a product. There is no
        App Store listing, no waitlist and no release date, because none of that exists yet.
      </p>
    </header>

    <ol class="grid">
      {
        phases.map((phase) => (
          <li class="card">
            <span class={`badge badge--${phase.tone}`}>
              <span class="badge__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              {phase.state}
            </span>
            <h3 class="t-card-title">{phase.title}</h3>
            <p class="t-secondary">{phase.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <p class="t-caption measure">
      If you would like to hear when there is something to try: there is no sign-up form here on
      purpose — an email address you typed into a static page has nowhere safe to go until the service
      above exists.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
